{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "CMS to prioritise reclaiming & repayment of overpayments made in error",
        "additional_details": "We believe the CMS is not fit for purpose, and we feel that's apparent to anyone that deals with them. By targeting one small change at a time perhaps A big change can be achieved. A lack of repercussions for misleading the CMS or pleading ignorance regarding CMS mistakes can benefit receiving parents. We\u2019re concerned that this may be leading to intentional deception and gaining more in payments. Currently the CMS has no system in place for returning overpayments, and there are no repercussions for receiving parents submitting fraudulent claims. There should be equally robust action to reclaim & repay overpaid money as to enforce payments in the first place.",
        "background": "The CMS use robust enforcement measures to claim payments even during disputes which are causing serious distress for paying parents. The same approach should be used to reclaim & then repay overpayments made as a result of CMS calculation errors and false information supplied by receiving parents.",
